---
title: "unstrung Videos"
description: "Videos showing the unstrung app in use, from the eyesunstrung YouTube channel."
contentsPanel: true
---
{#- Built from content/_data/videos.json, which scripts/fetch-videos.mjs fetches
    from YouTube (npm run fetch:videos). Newest video first.
    Players are embedded with enablejsapi=1, so assets/js/videos.js can pause a
    video when its disclosure closes and set its speed, and rel=0, so suggested
    videos at the end come only from this channel. The speed control is hidden
    until videos.js shows it, since it does nothing without the script. -#}
{{ videos.channel.description | paragraphs | safe }}
<p>All of these are on the <a href="{{ videos.channel.url }}">{{ videos.channel.name }} YouTube channel</a>.</p>
{% for video in videos.videos %}
<h2>{{ video.title }}</h2>
{{ video.description | paragraphs | safe }}
<details class="video">
  <summary>Watch {{ video.title }}</summary>
  <label class="video-speed" hidden>Playback speed
    <select>
      <option value="0.5">0.5 times</option>
      <option value="0.75">0.75 times</option>
      <option value="1">Normal</option>
      <option value="1.25">1.25 times</option>
      <option value="1.5">1.5 times</option>
      <option value="1.75">1.75 times</option>
      <option value="2">2 times</option>
    </select>
  </label>
  <iframe id="player-{{ video.id }}" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ video.id }}?enablejsapi=1&amp;rel=0" title="{{ video.title }}" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</details>
{% endfor %}
<script src="/assets/js/videos.js" defer></script>
